# Media and Cloudinary

## Configuration

- **Cloud name:** `dck5rzi4h`
- **Base path:** `art/moisestech-website/`
- **Asset folders:** `artworks/`, `exhibitions/`, `events/`, `own-your-digital-presence/`, `tech-nonprofit/`

## Data Sources

- Artwork images: `src/constants/artworks.ts`
- Exhibition images: `src/constants/exhibitions.ts`
- Eyebeam inquiry: `src/constants/eyebeam-inquiry.ts`
- Research: `src/constants/research.ts`, `noisy-systems.ts`
- Workshop images: `src/components/page/OoliteDigitalOverviewPage.tsx`, `TechNonprofitNavOolite.tsx`

## Image URLs

- Format: `https://res.cloudinary.com/dck5rzi4h/image/upload/v{version}/art/moisestech-website/...`
- Folder pattern: `artworks/{year}_{slug}/` (e.g., `artworks/2025_privacy_mask/`)

## When to Use Cloudinary MCP

- **Asset audit:** Compare Cloudinary assets to URLs in constants; find orphaned or missing assets
- **Tagging:** Add tags by artwork slug, year, exhibition
- **Organization:** Move assets into folders, rename for consistency
- **Transformations:** Generate optimized URLs (w_1200, q_auto, f_auto) for delivery

## Next.js Config

- `next.config.js` already allows `res.cloudinary.com` in `remotePatterns` and `domains`
- `images.unoptimized: true` is currently set — consider Cloudinary loader for optimization
